Z||000000||fiero_nightmare||10-27-2001||10:23 PM||||after i found out that it would cost too much to rebuild and beef up a 2.8 i have decided to just do a engine swap. i was thinking of doing a quad 4 conversion but i heard from ALOT of people that quad 4's go through heads like they were made of plastic. what i need to know is what is the cheapest/easiest engine swap there is that will give me more horsepower and torque then my 2.8? <P>it doesn't have to be too much faster just a little. <BR><P>------------------<BR>my 85 GT pics <P>http://communities.msn.com/russcars/85fierogt.msnw||||reg||5
Z||000001||Spektrum-87GT||10-27-2001||10:45 PM||||sounds like the 3.4 is perfect for you. either of them in fact, the pushrod or the dohc. the pushrod is much easier, i've heard its just like putting in a 2.8 only new starter holes have to be drilled, there maybe more. dohc is harder, mainly electrical. You can find good info on both using search. the pushrod makes 160hp, the dohc can make up to 215. good luck with whatever you choose.||||reg||1
Z||000002||lowCG||10-28-2001||11:47 AM||||I'd take a look at the accessories on your 2.8;how are the exhaust parts,alternator,wiring harness,etc.<BR>These parts all get replaced with newer stuff on the tdc swap,but it just could be wasted time/effort if those parts are already in great shape on your car now,since there's more time involved in the tdc swap.<BR>Also,some people can't get used to driving a car with the powerband above 3,000rpm;can be annoying,the 12 valve V-6 is going to be alot torquier,sooner,where the tdc will take off and scream a little later.<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||pontiacs4me||10-28-2001||10:19 PM||||first off Im going to explain to you what happens when you begin to mod a car.  at first, say you have a 2.8, its pretty fast stock, but you need more.  what youve done is desensitize yourself to speed, and you need to mod it.  drop in a 3.4, man this thing is fast, but after awhile you become used to the performance and it feels like it did with the 2.8.  You dont get the rush anymore, so you decide to mod some more.  in the long run it costs you thousands to go fast then faster.  I believe its best off to just start off with the faster.  <BR>My .02 go 3800 supercharged series II.  There is a huge aftermarked in the up and coming, and tons of bolt ons that arent available now will be soon  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  The initial cost will be more than a 3.4, but it will pay for itself in the long run.  A 3.4 only has so much.  I think the 3800 has so much more.  (no flame intended to 3.4 guys)||||reg||1
Z||000004||samoht||10-29-2001||11:44 AM||||3800 is the way to go.. But I did a 3.2 conversion, and it is reliable and easy rebiuld.. lost of threads.. push you will have a brand new motor.. I am happy with mine and no mod required...  I mean it is a basic steal head 3.1 rebuild only you have a 0/0 crank to start with..  3800 will be twice as much to rebuild.. plus new exhaust.. but but 225 HP easy.. I think I am pushing 200 from my 3.2 ....  headers I am sure woulme to 225<P>85gt3.2||||reg||1
Z||000005||Butter||10-29-2001||03:21 PM||||fiero_nightmare<P>Just Think.<P>Wow, I could've had a V8!<P>||||reg||11
Z||000006||mrfixit58||10-29-2001||04:55 PM||||Keep in mind that all motor swaps have trade-offs. A lot of people will po-po MPG but if the car is your daily driver and you used to getting 20+ MPG, a V-8 will cost more. I just bring it up for you to keep it in mind. We all would love to have 450 HP on tap but the thought of 10 MPG on a daily driver is insane.<P>Most of the time, the more cubic displacement, the worse the MPG. The real exception is the 3800 family. This motor, whether normally aspirated or supercharged, will get you better MPGs and still deliver butt puckering performance. The only down side is the up-front expense and difficulty level of the installation.<P>I've always thought that the best all around motor swap for the Fiero is the SC 3800. It'll get 20-30 MPG, blow away most Rustangs, and deliver carefree dependability.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||6
